## Motivation

JIT kernel benchmarks currently span ~4 divergent styles (triton `perf_report`, hand-rolled `perf_counter` loops, `marker` function-form, distributed). This standardizes them on the existing `marker` harness so every bench: (1) declares a torch reference for correctness, (2) sweeps config permutations, (3) reports the same way — and adds seeding, measured roofline, and an enforcement gate so the style can't drift.

## What's in this PR

**`marker.Kernel` contract** — a class declares three seams; the harness owns the rest:
```python
@marker.parametrize("dim", [1024, 4096], ci_vals=[4096])
@marker.kernel("impl", ["aot", "jit", "torch"], reference="torch")
class ActivationMul:
    def inputs(self, dim): return marker.io(create_random(dim))
    def run(self, impl, x): ...
```
